msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:453
msgid "bleed"
msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:453
msgid "``(float, 0–1)`` **Chroma bleed / fringing.** Horizontal chroma shift + blur with a slight desaturation. Gives the “rainbow edge” look."
msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:454
#: ../effects.rst:1240
msgid "softness"
msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:454
msgid "``(float, 0–1)`` **Luma softness.** Small horizontal blur on Y (approx. 0–2 px). Keep low to retain detail when noise is high."
msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:455
msgid "noise"
msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:455
msgid "``(float, 0–1)`` **Snow, hiss, and dropouts.** Controls grain strength, probability/length of white **streaks**, and a faint line hum."
msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:456
msgid "stripe"
msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:456
msgid "``(float, 0–1)`` **Tracking stripe.** Lifts the bottom band, adds hiss/noise there, and widens the lifted region as the value increases."
msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:457
msgid "static_bands"
msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:457
msgid "``(float, 0–1)`` **Static bursts.** Short bright bands with **row-clumped streaks** (many “shooting stars” across neighboring rows)."
msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:458
msgid "seed_offset"
msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:458
msgid "``(int, 0–1000)`` Adds to the internal seed (derived from the effect ID) for deterministic variation between clips."
msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:461
#: ../effects.rst:1252
#: ../effects.rst:1629
msgid "**Usage notes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:463
msgid "**Subtle “home video”**: ``tracking=0.25``, ``bleed=0.20``, ``softness=0.20``, ``noise=0.25``, ``stripe=0.10``, ``static_bands=0.05``."
msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:464
msgid "**Bad tracking / head clog**: ``tracking=0.8–1.0``, ``stripe=0.6–0.9``, ``noise=0.6–0.8``, ``static_bands=0.4–0.6``, ``softness<=0.2``, and set ``bleed`` to about 0.3."
msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:465
msgid "**Color fringing only**: raise ``bleed`` (about 0.5) and keep other controls low."
msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:466
msgid "**Different but repeatable snow**: leave the effect ID alone (for deterministic output) and change ``seed_offset`` to get a new, still-repeatable pattern."
msgstr ""

#: ../effects.rst:470
msgid "The Alpha Mask / Wipe Transition effect leverages a grayscale mask to create a dynamic transition between two images or video clips. In this effect, the light areas of the mask reveal the new image, while the dark areas conceal it, allowing for creative and custom transitions that go beyond standard fade or wipe techniques. This effect only affects the image, and not the audio track."
msgstr ""

